      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing an Image Provider**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud Vision API for generating image descriptions. The next step is to figure out the best way to incorporate the API into the `describe_image.py` script and make it easily identifiable.\n\n\n**Implementing the Google API**\n\nI am now focusing on writing the Python code for `describe_image.py`. I'm starting by including necessary imports and laying out the logic for calling the Google Cloud Vision API. I'm adding a placeholder for authentication, assuming `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` is set.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789859851112,
          "start": 1789859848376
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bbf5e0b8001M4Qw40ijyDRt8N",
